9. MENTOR WORKSPACE AND CALLING ENGINE
=====================================================
9.1 NUMBER MASKING (all devices): phones are masked (XXXXXX4521) for non-admin users on desktop, laptop and mobile, in the UI AND in every API response (server-side; CSS hiding is not enough). The real number is returned ONLY by POST /api/call-sessions/start, after the server confirms the target is assigned to this mentor (task.mentor_id = me, or enrollment.mentor_id = me) and writes an UNMASK audit log. Responses are Cache-Control: no-store. The number is cleared from client state when the popup closes. Admin screens show full numbers. Mentor APIs return only needed fields (no Govt ID, address, email, DOB).

9.2 CALL BUTTONS: each row shows masked Primary and Alternate/WhatsApp numbers, each with its own "Call" button (hide a button if that number is missing). If one number fails, the mentor tries the other.
Click flow: disable the button while the request runs (debounce) -> POST start with an idempotency key -> Call Popup opens with: student card (9.10), full number in large text, a "Dial now" tel:<prefix+number> button, neutral live timer, Disposition, Campaign Outcome (when the call belongs to a campaign), Remark (ALWAYS EMPTY on open), optional Reminder date + time, Submit. On mobile, also open the native dialer (tel:) as soon as the response arrives, and keep the popup so the mentor can return and enter the remark; the "Dial now" button is the fallback if the browser blocks auto-dial. Desktop/laptop: show the number for desk-phone dialing, no auto-dial.
Dispositions: Connected, Busy, No Answer, Switched Off, Not Reachable, Wrong Number, Callback Requested.

9.3 TIMER AND NO DUPLICATES: first_initiated_at is stored on the SERVER; the API returns server time so the timer never depends on the browser clock. Refreshing or reopening resumes the same timer. Clicking Call while a session is OPEN resumes it and never restarts. Using the other number or an explicit "Log Another Attempt" adds a CallAttempt inside the SAME CallLog (that attempt gets its own timer). A student called twice in one day = ONE row (database unique key) with 2 attempts. Reports show both "Calls" and "Attempts". An OPEN session that was never submitted is marked ABANDONED at midnight IST and shown to admin as "unsubmitted session"; it does not count as a call.

9.4 ASSIGNED CALLS (one list, filter chips; each task in exactly one chip; precedence top to bottom):
 - Called Today: any task/student with a CallLog today (all dispositions). Shows disposition, time, and TODAY'S OWN remark, with buttons "Update Today's Call" and "Log Another Attempt". It does NOT vanish after submit.
 - Reminders Due: PENDING reminder with remind_at <= now (stays visible, with its date, even if days late).
 - Pending: ASSIGNED and older than the threshold (Overdue badge), or ATTEMPTED on an earlier day with no future reminder (Retry badge).
 - New: ASSIGNED, within the threshold.
 Columns: Assigned Date, Campaign Purpose, Student, Batch, masked contacts, Status, Call buttons. After midnight a COMPLETED task leaves this list and goes to Call History (full detail stays with admin). A task with a future reminder is hidden until the reminder is due. Pending calls stay with the mentor. Assigned external leads appear here too, tagged "Lead" (name, city/school, and the lead's "note from sheet").

9.5 UPDATE TODAY'S CALL (parent calls back): available until 11:59:59 PM IST of the call's day. The mentor can change the disposition (e.g. No Answer -> Connected), ADD a new timestamped remark, change or clear the reminder, set the outcome. It edits the SAME CallLog, creates no new row, and starts no timer unless "Log Another Attempt" is chosen. Nothing is overwritten: every change is appended to CallActivity, so admin sees the original attempt, original disposition and remark, the callback update, new disposition, new remark and exact timestamps. Task status is recalculated. After midnight the API rejects edits and the UI hides the button permanently; if a reminder was set, the student returns on that date and a fresh call is logged then.

9.6 REMARK PRIVACY (enforced in a DTO/query layer for every mentor endpoint, with tests): a mentor receives remark text only if it was written by THEM and TODAY (IST). No "remark" column exists in any mentor list. Never any remark from earlier days, other mentors, or admin. The new-call form is always empty; the update form shows today's earlier notes read-only plus an empty box for a new remark. Admin sees the complete chronological history.

9.7 STEALTH ANTI-CHEAT: mentors see only a neutral timer, no hint about timing anywhere. REMOVE completely every client message like "Anti-Cheat Alert / Suspicious Instant Submission". On server submit: if disposition = Connected and (submitted_at - latest attempt started_at) < suspicious_seconds (default 15, hidden setting), silently store latency_seconds and is_suspicious_submission = TRUE. No mentor-facing API response may contain latency or the flag. An INBOUND_UPDATE (no dialing) is not latency-checked; admin audit shows its "minutes after the original call". Flags appear only in admin audit screens and admin Excel exports. Note in the README: the timer measures time since dialer initiation, not verified phone conversation time.

9.8 MY STUDENTS: only students whose Enrollment.mentor_id = me (matched from the upload's Mentor column), ALL of them, server-paginated with "Showing X-Y of TOTAL" (e.g. 120 students = all 120 across pages). Columns: Student, Batch, masked Primary + Alternate with Call buttons, attendance summary, latest result. NO assignment date and NO remarks here. A mentor may call anyone here voluntarily at any time (creates a CallLog without a task). Students with an ACTIVE task appear only in Assigned Calls; show "Total X students | Y currently in Assigned Calls". Filter chip "Monthly Call Due". After a task completes, the student shows here again.

9.9 CALL HISTORY (mentor): own completed calls (date/time, student, batch, disposition), remarks only if written today. Reminder and history dates/times are fully visible, never clipped (D5 format; cards on mobile).

9.10 STUDENT CARD (inside popup and student view, read-only): overall attendance %, subject-wise "Physics: 18/20 classes present", expandable Absent list (date, time slot, subject), latest exam result subject-wise with rank.

9.11 MONTHLY RULE: every student owned by a mentor needs a Connected call at least every 30 days (D10). Overdue students appear for the mentor as "Monthly Call Due" (in Reminders Due and My Students) and are counted on the admin dashboard. Computed by an indexed query (no mass reminder rows). An unattempted assignment never counts as a relationship call.

9.12 REMINDERS: optional date + time (time defaults to 10:00 AM). A new call to the same student marks earlier PENDING reminders DONE; changing a reminder in an update marks the old one CLEARED.

