12. SECURITY
=====================================================
Real protection is server-side: role check on EVERY API and in every DB query filter, server-masked numbers, field whitelists, audit logs (views, unmasks, exports), rate limits, httpOnly cookies, CSRF/origin checks, security headers (CSP, X-Frame-Options, no-referrer), no stack traces to clients.
Browser deterrents for NON-ADMIN only (admin is exempt): user-select:none, block right-click, block Ctrl+C/X/A/U/S/P, F12 and PrintScreen keys, @media print hides content, blur the screen when the tab/window loses focus, diagonal watermark on every data screen with Mentor Name + ID + live timestamp.
README must state honestly: a browser cannot truly block OS-level screenshots or screen recording; these measures are deterrents plus traceability (a native app is needed for a hard block).

=====================================================
13. PERFORMANCE
=====================================================
Every list is server-paginated (25/50/100/200, default 50), searched (debounced 300 ms) and sorted server-side, always showing "Showing X-Y of TOTAL"; NO 50-record cap on total accessible data. Bulk imports use batched INSERT ... ON CONFLICT (1,000 rows per batch) in transactions; no N+1 queries; heavy stats are never computed on page load (attendance summaries precomputed at upload, last_connected_at stored on the row, Pending/Overdue via indexed queries). Must stay smooth with 30 simultaneous users and 50,000+ enrollments.

=====================================================
14. UI RULES (simple, like a Google Sheet)
=====================================================
Spreadsheet-style grids: sticky header, column search/filter, sortable, resizable columns, keyboard friendly. Big buttons, plain words, minimal colors, no animations. Responsive: on screens under 768 px mentor lists become cards. Date/time cells never clipped (no ellipsis; nowrap; auto width). Real empty states ("No records") and loading states; no fake counts. Buttons that cannot act are removed, not disabled-forever.

